# Flutter Mobile Standards

- Follow feature-first folder layout (`lib/features/<name>/`)
- Keep widgets small; extract private `_Widget` classes for subtrees
{{#if parameters.constWidgets}}
- Use `const` constructors wherever possible to reduce rebuilds
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.useRiverpod}}
- Use Riverpod providers for app state; avoid `setState` in large widgets
- Prefer `AsyncValue` for loading/error/data UI states
{{else}}
- Use `ChangeNotifier` or BLoC consistently within a feature; do not mix patterns
{{/if}}
- Platform channels only when plugins are insufficient; document channel contracts
{{#if parameters.goldenTests}}
- Add golden tests for key screens; update goldens intentionally in PRs
{{/if}}
- Run `dart format` and `flutter analyze` before commit
